2 has pop)\n   - Movie: superhero (from constraint 1)\n\n   Now assign the remaining movie genre: Person 1 must have spy.\n\n   Final assignments:\n\n   **Person 1:**\n   - Beverage: cola\n   - Movie: spy\n   - Music: classical\n\n   **Person 2:**\n   - Beverage: mirinda\n   - Movie: superhero\n   - Music: pop\n\n   Let’s verify constraints:\n\n   1. Superhero is immediately right of classical → Person 2 has superhero, Person 1 has classical → ✅\n\n   2. Pop is not the same as cola → Person 2 has pop and mirinda, Person 1 has cola and classical → pop and cola are on different people → ✅\n\n   All attributes are uniquely assigned → ✅\n\n   Now answer the questions:\n\n   **1. What is the movie genre of the person who drinks mirinda?**  \n   → Person 2 drinks mirinda → Movie = superhero → **superhero**\n\n   **2. At what position is the person who drinks mirinda?**  \n   → Person 2 → **2**\n\n   **3. What movie genre does the person who listens to classical watch?**  \n   → Person 1 listens to classical → Movie = spy → **spy**\n\n   **4. What music genre does the person who drinks cola listen to?**  \n   → Person 1 drinks cola → Music = classical → **classical**\n\n   So the four answers in order are:\n   - superhero\n   - 2\n   - spy\n   - classical\n\nFinal answer: <solution>superhero, 2, spy, classical</solution>", "logprobs": [{"token": "We", "logprob": -0.03804187476634979}, {"token": " are", "logprob": -0.0789945125579834}, {"token": " told", "logprob": -0.8259409070014954}, {"token": " there", "logprob": -0.08271192759275436}, {"token": " are", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " two", "logprob": -0.48546189069747925}, {"token": " people", "logprob": -2.0265558760002023e-06}, {"token": " in", "logprob": -0.003437564242631197}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -8.272782724816352e-05}, {"token": " line", "logprob": -1.1920922133867862e-06}, {"token": ",", "logprob": -0.0015148365637287498}, {"token": " numbered", "logprob": -0.012855041772127151}, {"token": " ", "logprob": -0